## Business-Outcome Story
Household food budgets are under sustained pressure. The average American family of four now spends between $150–$250 per week on groceries depending on meal planning discipline. The gap between undisciplined and disciplined spending is almost entirely attributable to the absence of structured, pre-committed weekly planning. This project closes that gap for dinner — the highest-cost and highest-effort meal of the day.

The Family Dinner Planner delivers a concrete, cost-verified 7-night dinner schedule for a family of four within a hard $120 ceiling. It is not a recipe website, a subscription box, or a general meal inspiration tool. It is a planning artifact with a measurable financial commitment.

## Market Context
Meal planning tools exist in abundance (Mealime, Plan to Eat, Paprika), but they optimise for convenience and variety, not hard budget enforcement. The budget-constrained family segment — households actively tracking weekly grocery spend — is underserved by tools that surface recipes without cost accountability. This planner is positioned as a **budget-first, dinner-specific planning instrument**, not a lifestyle product.

## Competitive Frame
| Dimension | Generic Meal Planners | This Planner |
|---|---|---|
| Budget enforcement | Soft / optional | Hard ceiling ($120) |
| Scope | All meals | Dinners only |
| Output | Recipe list | Costed shopping list + schedule |
| Allergen handling | Variable | Disclosed per meal |
| Pantry assumption | Rarely modelled | Explicitly excluded from cost |

## Stakeholder Map
| Stakeholder | Role | Interest |
|---|---|---|
| Primary Cook | End user | Practical, executable plan |
| Household Budget Holder | Approver | Cost compliance |
| Family Members (×4) | Consumers | Variety, palatability, safety |
| Allergen-Sensitive Members | Risk stakeholder | Accurate allergen disclosure |

## Milestones
| Month | Milestone |
|---|---|
| M0 | Objective locked: $120 / 7 dinners / family of four |
| M1 | Recipe pool selected and cost-estimated against current market prices |
| M1 | Pantry exclusion list finalised and documented |
| M2 | Full 7-day schedule produced with per-meal cost breakdown |
| M2 | Consolidated shopping list generated and allergen flags reviewed |
| M2 | Total estimated cost validated at ≤ $120 — plan ready for execution |

## Investment Ask
This is a planning and coordination effort, not a capital project. Primary resource investment is time: approximately 2–4 hours for initial plan construction, recurring at approximately 30–60 minutes per week for re-use and adaptation. No external vendor spend is required. (assumed)

